IO-33: report misspelt [FILES] and [REPORT] keywords (ERROR 205)

handle_files() skipped a [FILES] line whose mode was not SAVE or USE and
ignored an unknown file type, and handle_report() ignored an unknown
[REPORT] keyword, all without a message. Legacy SWMM reports each as
ERROR 205 (on platforms where char is signed). They are now ERROR 205
naming the word. A word is unknown when it does not begin with one of the
legacy keywords, since legacy findmatch() matches prefixes; NO and SCRATCH
remain valid [FILES] modes that name no file, so nothing legacy accepts is
refused.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-33_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/ControlsHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/ControlsHandler.cpp
index 9c02553..46dd372 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/ControlsHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/ControlsHandler.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@
 #include "../Tokenizer.hpp"
 #include "../../core/SimulationContext.hpp"
 #include "../../data/InfraData.hpp"
+#include "../../core/ErrorCodes.hpp"
 
 #include <string>
 
@@ -173,6 +174,15 @@ void handle_report(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& lines
         else if (keyword == "DISABLED") {
             ctx.options.rpt_disabled = Tokenizer::parse_boolean(tok[1]);
         }
+        else {
+            // legacy report_readOptions(): a keyword that does not begin with
+            // one of its report words is ERROR 205 (findmatch() matches a prefix)
+            static const char* const words[] = {"DISABLED", "INPUT", "SUBCATCH",
+                "NODE", "LINK", "CONTINUITY", "FLOWSTATS", "CONTROLS", "AVERAGES"};
+            bool known = false;
+            for (const char* w : words) known = known || keyword.rfind(w, 0) == 0;
+            if (!known) ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[0]));
+        }
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/FilesHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/FilesHandler.cpp
